  "body": "**Stacked on #1002** (the #926 per-post script suites, whose recorded `rotary` golden pins this fix). This branch carries #1002's commit plus a merge of upstream `main`; merge #1002 first, then this PR's diff is only the #997 change. Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe RTCP path of `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` wrote all three angle words on the arm block whatever the machine stated - on the A+B tilthead, `G00 X0 Y0 Z20 A30 B0 C0`. A control with no C axis alarms on the C address (or, where C is another function, commands it).\n\n- `statesRotary(letter)` reads `machine.rotaries`; `angleWord(letter, v)` writes a word only for a stated rotary. The arm block and the modal changed-letter words both go through it. Arm on the tilthead is now `G00 X0 Y0 Z20 A30 B0`.\n- `missingLetter` (now built on `statesRotary`) still runs first, so a **turning** letter of an absent rotary stays refused by name (`tilted move commands C - the machine states no C rotary`). The only letters dropped are stated zeros.\n- **Other posts checked:** haas, mazak, sinumerik, heidenhain and carvera refuse a tilted stream outright (no RTCP output); tormach writes A only on its own index path; fanuc-lathe / tormach-lathe refuse posed moves. Only `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps` shared the bug (its RTCP path is a copy of fanuc's) - fixed here the same way.\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/997-absent-rotary-word.md`.\n\n## Goldens\n\n- New: `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/fanuc/rotary.nc` (read before commit: G43.4 arm, `A30 B0`, modal `A0 B30`, return `B0`, no C word anywhere); the `(\"fanuc.cps\", \"rotary\", 997)` line is removed from `KNOWN_BUGS`.\n- Every other golden is byte-identical (no `.nc`/`.refusal`/`.cl` file changed). doosan-dnm's recorded `rotary` stays its refusal (no clamp codes declared), unchanged.\n- One existing assertion changed: `fanuc_post::rtcp_output_arms_once_and_walks_the_angles` asserted `G00 X10 Y0 Z5 A40 B0 C0` on an **A-only** trunnion - it had pinned the bug. It now asserts `G00 X10 Y0 Z5 A40`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `script_fanuc::rotary` (the #926 recorded golden)\n- `fanuc_post::an_absent_rotary_takes_no_angle_word` (tilthead: arm `A30 B0`, modal `A0 B30`, no C word; a turning C refused by name)\n- `doosan_dnm_post::doosan_dnm_absent_rotary_takes_no_angle_word`\n\nGate (macOS, local, worktree target/, sccache):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: post suites (lib, axis_direction_cli, comp, comp_plane, mch_head_search, post_engine, recorded_streams, every script_*) ok; app doosan_dnm_post, recorded_post_streams ok; fanuc_post failed once on the old word-count assertion below, fixed, then the whole `fanuc_post` suite 12/12 ok.\n- App suites, whole: posting 17, golden_cl 25, conformance 6, tilt 8, fanuc_post 12, doosan_dnm_post 8, fourth_axis_pose 9, rotary_verify 9, recorded_post_streams 2 - all ok.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n`rtcp_output_arms_once_and_walks_the_angles` also asserted the modal block had fewer words than the arm block; on an A-only machine both now carry the single A word, so that comparison is dropped (the exact-line asserts still pin both blocks, and the modal law - unchanged angles rest, only the changed letter returns - is pinned by the new `fanuc/rotary.nc` golden: `G01 X20 Y0 Z0 F800`, `G00 X20 Y20 Z50 B0`).\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo hand-post on a real machine; the doosan fix is pinned only by its direct test (its recorded `rotary` case refuses earlier on undeclared clamp codes).\n\nChangelog: Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts no longer write an angle word (e.g. C0) for a rotary the machine does not state (#997)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #997\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
